schema: "0.4"
id: fim-math-and-scientific-rendering-chemdraw-js-02-substructure-reaction-stress
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: chemdraw-js
category: math-and-scientific-rendering
variant: substructure-reaction-stress
references:
- references/fim/solution/chemdraw-js.md
- references/fim/use-case/mathematical-scientific.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior cheminformatics visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML document with inline CSS and JavaScript. Use RDKit.js-compatible SMILES, SMARTS, reaction SMILES, SVG rendering, and explicit WASM cleanup. No Markdown fences or explanatory prose outside the artifact.
  text: |-
    Create a dense chemistry analysis artifact that stress-tests RDKit.js substructure highlighting, reaction rendering, and small-molecule comparison.

    Scenario:
    Build an interactive chemistry worksheet comparing aspirin, acetaminophen, caffeine, ibuprofen, and salicylic acid. Render each molecule as an RDKit SVG, highlight a selected SMARTS functional group, show descriptor deltas, and render a simple esterification reaction scheme when supported.

    Requirements:
    - Include a fixed molecule dataset with name, SMILES, short use note, and expected functional groups.
    - Provide SMARTS options for carboxyl, phenyl ring, hydroxyl, amide, ester, and carbonyl query patterns.
    - Use RDKit.get_qmol for SMARTS queries and mol.get_substruct_match or equivalent matching before calling get_svg_with_highlights.
    - Use highlight colors as RGB floats from 0 to 1, not hex or 0-255 values.
    - Include a reaction SMILES panel for CC(=O)O.OCC>>CC(=O)OCC.O and use RDKit.get_rxn when available; if unavailable, render reactants and products separately with a clear fallback note.
    - Compute descriptors for every valid molecule and show a compact comparison table.
    - Delete every mol, qmol, and rxn object created.
    - Include invalid SMARTS and invalid SMILES handling paths visible in the UI.
    - Keep the dense view readable with wrapping cards, concise labels, and no overlapping structures.
    - Output only the final HTML artifact.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 10000
    temperature: 0.25
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: rdkit-substructure-reaction-workbook
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: svg
  render_expectation: Browser worksheet with multiple RDKit molecule SVGs, SMARTS highlighting, descriptor table, and reaction rendering or fallback.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and the generated output is one ASCII HTML artifact with no Markdown fences."
  - "The dataset includes aspirin, acetaminophen, caffeine, ibuprofen, and salicylic acid with valid SMILES."
  - "SMARTS queries use RDKit.get_qmol and are not confused with SMILES molecule parsing."
  - "Substructure highlighting uses matched atom or bond indices from the same molecule and RGB float colors."
  - "Reaction SMILES uses get_rxn when available and provides a clear fallback when the RDKit build lacks reaction support."
  - "Descriptors are computed for each valid molecule and comparison values remain aligned with the rendered structures."
  - "Every RDKit mol, qmol, and rxn object is deleted after use."
  - "Invalid molecule/query inputs show visible errors without breaking the rest of the worksheet."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Generated HTML and JavaScript are syntactically coherent and use RDKit.js APIs from the reference."
    - "The reaction, molecule, and query code paths are distinguishable and correctly typed."
    - "The artifact can render without requiring commercial ChemDraw JS."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "All requested molecules, SMARTS options, descriptors, and reaction scheme behavior are present."
    - "The worksheet demonstrates substructure matching, highlighting, comparison, and reaction rendering or fallback."
    - "Invalid input handling is part of the UI, not only comments."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Molecule cards, highlights, descriptor table, and reaction panel are readable in a dense layout."
    - "Highlight colors are distinguishable and do not obscure bond or atom labels."
    - "The comparison table is compact, aligned, and easy to scan."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles unsupported get_rxn, invalid SMARTS, invalid SMILES, empty matches, and descriptor parse failures."
    - "Avoids WASM memory leaks by deleting all RDKit objects."
    - "Keeps the page usable when one molecule or query fails."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, and Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in SMARTS handling, highlight indexing, reaction fallback, or cleanup."
  - "A reviewer can verify wide output-space coverage across molecule rendering, query matching, descriptors, and reaction visualization."
tags:
- fim
- math-and-scientific-rendering
- chemdraw-js
- rdkit-js
- smarts
- reaction-smiles
- substructure-highlighting
- stress
